Memory leak: prerender-interrupt Error kept as AbortSignal.reason retains its V8 stack frames, pinning the whole render closure graph

### Summary

A prerender-interrupt `Error` is stored as an `AbortSignal.reason` and never has its `.stack` read. V8 therefore keeps that Error's **structured stack trace** (the internal `FixedArray` of `CallSiteInfo`) alive, and every retained frame pins the frame's function → its `Context` → **the entire closure graph of the render that created it**, including the cached page value and its `segmentData` buffers.

Net effect in production: one aborted render pins one page's worth of memory, permanently. Our two app replicas grow ≈ **+0.45 GB/hour**, linearly, until the kernel cgroup-OOM-kills them every 9–10 hours.

This is very likely the root cause of the symptom already reported in #84648 ("Memory leak during load tests in dynamic rendering mode" — memory stays at ~15 GB after a load test and never drops). That issue has an app-level reproduction but no diagnosis; this issue is the diagnosis.

