LLVM assumes that calls to the global allocator (and [local variable cration](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/162214#issuecomment-5523138830)) do not fail when trying to optimize away unused allocations. This results in calls that are always going to fail (because they together exceed the address space) being able to observably violate invariants of rust types, for example by making `&mut`s provably overlap.

