Avoid acquiring asyncio_tasks_lock when the thread-local task list is empty

# Bug report

### Bug description:

In function void PyThreadState_Clear(PyThreadState *tstate)：
```python
......
    PyMutex_Lock(&tstate->interp->asyncio_tasks_lock);
    // merge any lingering tasks from thread state to interpreter's
    // tasks list
    llist_concat(&tstate->interp->asyncio_tasks_head,
                 &((_PyThreadStateImpl *)tstate)->asyncio_tasks_head);
    PyMutex_Unlock(&tstate->interp->asyncio_tasks_lock);
......
```

This path may be executed even when the thread has no locally registered
asyncio tasks. The current implementation still performs an atomic mutex
operation in that case.

Proposed change is to check the thread-local list before acquiring the lock:
```python
......
    struct llist_node *local_head =
    &((_PyThreadStateImpl *)tstate)->asyncio_tasks_head;

    if (!llist_empty(local_head)) {
        PyMutex_Lock(&tstate->interp->asyncio_tasks_lock);
        llist_concat(&tstate->interp->asyncio_tasks_head, local_head);
        PyMutex_Unlock(&tstate->interp->asyncio_tasks_lock);
    }
......
