Regression 1.98 → 1.99: `thread_local!` destructors no longer run at thread exit on `wasm32-wasip1-threads`

`thread_local!` destructors stopped running at thread exit on `wasm32-wasip1-threads` in Rust 1.99.0. Spawned threads that own a `thread_local!` value with a `Drop` impl leak it; the destructor never runs, not even after `JoinHandle::join` returns.

### Code

I tried this code:

```rust
use std::cell::Cell;
use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicUsize, Ordering};
use std::sync::Arc;

struct Probe(Arc<AtomicUsize>);
impl Drop for Probe {
    fn drop(&mut self) {
        self.0.fetch_add(1, Ordering::SeqCst);
    }
}

thread_local! {
    static PROBE: Cell<Option<Probe>> = const { Cell::new(None) };
}

fn main() {
    let completed = Arc::new(AtomicUsize::new(0));
    let n = 4;
    let handles: Vec<_> = (0..n)
        .map(|_| {
            let c = Arc::clone(&completed);
            std::thread::spawn(move || PROBE.with(|slot| slot.set(Some(Probe(c)))))
        })
        .collect();
    for h in handles {
        h.join().unwrap();
    }
    let seen = completed.load(Ordering::SeqCst);
    println!("threads={n} tls_destructors_ran={seen}");
    assert_eq!(seen, n, "TLS destructors did not run on wasm32-wasip1-threads");
}
