The report (below) was LLM generated, hope that's not an issue. It took 1200 runs to hone in on the exact problem, so it's not like I can do that manually :)

---

On Windows, a `TcpStream::try_clone()` taken right after `TcpStream::connect_timeout()` sometimes returns a handle that rejects `shutdown` with WSAENOTCONN (10057), although the connection is up. Every later shutdown on that clone fails the same way. A shutdown on the original handle succeeds, and the peer then sees EOF. After a blocking `TcpStream::connect()`, the clone never fails.

