Support masked environment variables in the Copilot Agent Host sandbox

## Feature request

Add a VS Code setting for choosing environment variables to mask inside the Copilot Agent Host sandbox and the HTTPS hosts allowed to receive their real values.

The SDK already accepts `sandboxConfig.credentials.envVars`, but VS Code does not currently expose or forward this configuration.

## Proposed configuration

Setting: `chat.agent.sandbox.maskedEnvironmentVariables`

Title: **Masked environment variables**

Description: Choose environment variables and the HTTPS hosts allowed to receive their real values.

```json
{
  "chat.agent.sandbox.maskedEnvironmentVariables": {
    "envVars": {
      "MY_API_TOKEN": {
        "injectHosts": ["api.example.com"]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Only environment variable names and destination mappings belong in settings, not secret values.

## Expected behavior

- Forward the configuration to local and remote Agent Hosts and the Copilot SDK when sandboxing is enabled.
- Apply it on session creation, resume, and subsequent turns.
- Clear configured mappings when the setting is reset.
- Preserve independent Git and GitHub authentication preferences and existing sandbox network restrictions.
- Leave credential masking, host-pattern validation, and injection enforcement to the runtime.

